course: dictionary
lesson: 15094
title: Rotational
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rotational means to do with turning round a centre point. A wheel, a fan or a clock hand all make rotational movement.
explain: In maths, a shape has rotational symmetry if it looks the same after a turn of less than a full turn. «A square looks the same after a quarter turn.»
explain: The order of rotational symmetry counts how many times the shape fits itself in one full turn. A square has order 4. Rotational can also mean taking turns in a fixed order, as in «a rotational timetable».
fact: Rotational means to do with turning round a centre point.
fact: «Rotational symmetry» means a shape looks the same after being turned less than a full turn.
fact: «Order of rotational symmetry» is how many times a shape matches itself in one full turn.
fact: A square has order 4, because it matches itself four times in a full turn.
fact: «A rotational timetable» means people take turns in a fixed order.
exercise: «The windmill blades make rotational movement as they spin.» What does rotational mean here? | Stopping suddenly | Moving in a straight line | *Turning round a centre point | Falling down
exercise: «A square has order 4 of rotational symmetry.» How many times does a square look the same in one full turn? | 2 | *4 | 3 | 1
exercise: «The class has a rotational timetable, so each group takes turns in the same order each week.» What does rotational suggest here? | *Taking turns in a fixed order | Being very fast | Going round a playground | Painting the walls
test: Which shape looks the same after a quarter turn? | Tall thin triangle | *Square | Random blob | Rectangle that is much longer than it is wide
test: Mrs Okafor writes «rotational farming» on the board. What does it mean? | *Growing crops in a fixed order, taking turns on each field | Painting the farm gate | Digging one big hole in the middle of a field | Turning the soil as fast as possible
exam: «The shape turns and looks the same four times in one full turn.» What is its order of rotational symmetry? | 2 | *4 | 8 | 1
